WHAT IT DOES. forced_v3_verdict adds a knife-edge row's three columns, in parentheses and '; '-joined, to the burst test's part
of the reason, in all three forms of it: after the evidence and the centroid for BACKGROUND SOURCE; after "no cataloged source
is identified as their emitter" for NOT CENTERED ON THE TARGET (source not identified); after the lower-cased verdict for every
other result. A row whose draws split carries the split in its verdict itself ("UNDECIDED (knife-edge: the method's random
draws split - <class> in a of 20, <class> in b of 20)"), which the figure prints lower-cased like any other verdict.
  mc_draws          a decided row's fraction: "CONSISTENT WITH A BACKGROUND SOURCE in 20 of 20 Monte Carlo draws; named: VLSSr
                    J105425.8+715204 in 20 of 20, VLSSr J105246.5+715924 in 19 of 20" (empty for a split row)
  named_knife_edge  every source named in an undecided fraction of the draws, never in the named set (nor in named_radec):
                    "knife-edge: VLSSr J213749.6+303900 named in 9 of 20 draws"
  knife_edge        the statistic that put the row on its threshold: "knife-edge: centroid z 3.02 vs 3, Monte Carlo error 0.017"
The verdicts' mapping (V3_MAP) is unchanged. A row without the columns, or with them empty (every unflagged row), gives exactly
today's (verdict, reason). The figures of a run show the text once they are redrawn after the republish (the figure step reads
the run's file when it draws).
